The glob view prints a CSS file's header comment; `//` lines aren't CSS comments, so they are no header.
== args
input
== file input/theme.css
/* Theme colors and fonts. */
:root {}
== file input/plain.css
.a {}
== file input/slashes.css
// Not a CSS comment.
.a {}
== stdout
glob view: input
input/plain.css (1 line): (no header available)
input/slashes.css (2 lines): (no header available)
input/theme.css (2 lines): Theme colors and fonts.
== stderr
== exit 0
